{"t": 44.485, "n": 56, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "All four verification commands came back clean in the preview, and I changed nothing after it.\n\nThe plan is `completed`, every row is marked, and `docs/tasks/i203a.report.md` is written. This visit I made no file edits, so there was nothing new to commit.\n\n- **Preview:** all four plan commands (engine pytest, engine `ruff check src tests`, engine `mypy`, package `pytest -q tests`) were reused from results recorded for this same tree. The check passed 14 of 14.\n- **Reading this visit:** I read these against the specs:\n  - `regeneration.py` in full, against `regeneration.spec.md` and `regeneration-failures.spec.md`;\n  - the `regeneration` unit in `workflow/temperspec/__init__.py` and its `blueprint.json` entry;\n  - the `checks.py` code that lists regeneration-written files;\n  - the prompt edits in `plan.md`, `expand.md` and `code.md`;\n  - the engine back gate, namely the `validate.py` finding codes, the `nodes.py` verdict, the `gate.py` reason lines and HUM-B15 to HUM-B18;\n  - `registry.py` `other_checkout` and the `verify.py` register rung;\n  - the assertions of `test_regeneration_run.py` and `test_gate_back.py`.\n\n  I found no place where the code disagrees with a spec.\n- **Deviations:** none new. The report lists the earlier ones, including the extra `\"proves\": \"EVS-AC7\"` key in the five fixtures and the third reason-line pin in `test_regeneration_run.py`.\n- **For the operator:** `stamp.json`, `authoring.json` and `diagram/` of `plugins/temperspec-tgraph` still need refreshing with `tempergraph author verify plugins/temperspec-tgraph`. No row edits them by hand, as the plan says.\n\nARTIFACT code_report: docs/tasks/i203a.report.md\nARTIFACT tests_passed: yes", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "460b6cc4-f348-48f4-9442-47cf94fb7355"}
